# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository regardless of the checking-out
# platform's git config (core.autocrlf) — without this, Windows checkouts convert text
# files to CRLF on checkout while tools like npm always write LF, so any `npm install`
# immediately shows package-lock.json (and similar generated files) as "modified" with
# no real content change. This was the root cause of git pull getting repeatedly blocked
# on a Linux deployment box after npm install had run there.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touched by line-ending normalization regardless, but explicit
# beats relying on text=auto's content-sniffing to get it right for every file type.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
